        "x": 60,
        "y": -170
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "### What this graph answers\n\nKenyon cells are the mushroom body's parallel fibres. This asks where they *receive* their\ninput: postsynapse counts per brain region, split by KC subtype.\n\nThe calyx should dominate the result. That expectation is the check on whether the pipeline is\ndoing what it claims.",
        "outline": true
      },
      "size": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 160
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step1",
      "type": "note.text",
      "position": {
        "x": 892,
        "y": 430
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "**One row per neuron and region.** The ROI node explodes each neuron into its per-region\ncounts, which is the shape the grouping then collapses. Two group keys go in, so what comes out\ncarries a region column, a type column and a summed count.",
        "outline": true
      },
      "size": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 130
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step2",
      "type": "note.text",
      "position": {
        "x": 1724,
        "y": 430
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "**Two keys make a stacked chart.** The chart reads region as the category, the summed count as\nthe value and type as the series — the three columns the grouping just produced. Change either\nkey and the chart follows.",
        "outline": true
      },
      "size": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 130
      }
